# --- Git Destructive & Force Operations ---
git reset --hard#Irreversible: Overwrites all local changes and matches the remote HEAD.
git rebase -i#Risk: Rewrites commit history; can cause complex conflicts in shared branches.
git clean -fd#Danger: Permanently removes untracked files and directories from your workspace.
git push --force#Critical: Overwrites remote history. Potential to delete colleagues work.
gpf#Alias for force-with-lease: Still risky as it pushes local history to remote.
gres#History manipulation: Soft reset can lead to messy staging area if not careful.
greb#Interactive rebase alias: High risk of losing work during conflict resolution.
gresh#Hard reset alias: Immediate loss of all uncommitted code.
gcl#Clean alias: Deletes untracked assets that might not be backed up.
gcanp#Amend + Force push: Double risk of rewriting local and remote history.
gacanp#Stage + Amend + Force push: Nukes current state and forces it to remote.

# --- System High-Risk & Permissions ---
chmod -R#Recursive permissions: Can break system security or render services unreadable.
chown -R#Recursive ownership: Can lock you out of your own files or break system daemons.
rm -rf#The Nuke: Permanently deletes files and folders without moving to trash.
mv /#Critical: Moving system root or top-level dirs will cause immediate system failure.
shred#Security: Overwrites file data multiple times; absolutely impossible to recover.
nuke#Alias for rm -rf node_modules: Dangerous if run in the wrong parent directory.

# --- Docker & Database Destruction ---
docker system prune#Cleanup: Deletes all stopped containers, unused networks, and dangling images.
docker volume rm#Data Loss: Permanently deletes persistent data stored in Docker volumes.
docker-compose down -v#Cleanup: Stops containers and removes all associated volumes (data loss).
dclean#Docker Nuke: Clears everything including non-dangling images and volumes.
dlt#Teardown: Destroys lab environment including persistent storage.
dlr#Reset: Full wipe and rebuild of the local development lab.
drmi#Cleanup: Removes images; might trigger re-downloading of large layers.
dropdb#Database: Permanently deletes the specified database and all its tables.

# --- System Services & Network ---
fwd#Firewall: Disabling UFW exposes your system to direct network attacks.
sstop#Service Stop: Stopping critical systemd units can hang the OS or crash apps.
cam-off#Hardware: Disables camera interface via kernel module or system toggle.
bt-off#Hardware: Disables Bluetooth stack; will disconnect all wireless peripherals.
